tags: usb-device-id, usb-id

The identity of the model of a USB device: two 16-bit numbers of its device
descriptor, which the maker of the device sets.

=== formal
class=concept
name=usb-device-id
product=the 16-bit number at bytes 10 and 11 of the device descriptor (idProduct), little-endian
text=<vendor>:<product>, each as 4 digits of base 16, with the letters a to f in lowercase
vendor=the 16-bit number at bytes 8 and 9 of the device descriptor (idVendor), little-endian
